{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"gleesome-hominine-merganser","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context\n\nThe account runs a daily Bedrock spend cap enforced by the `bedrock-spend-cap` Lambda. It has two tiers: a **warning** tier that publishes to the `bedrock-spend-cap-alerts` SNS topic, and a **hard** tier that attaches the `BedrockDailySpendCapDeny` IAM policy to the target roles. The hard tier has already tripped once (the Lambda's state parameter records `tripped_day: 2026-09-13`).\n\nAgents currently have no instruction covering the warning tier. When the warning fires, an agent that keeps running plan-review, code review, and completion gates drives spend toward the hard deny. If the hard tier trips, `BedrockDailySpendCapDeny` blocks Bedrock for every target role at once, which takes out the review bot and all gate operations for the remainder of the day — a self-inflicted outage in place of a voluntary slowdown.\n\nThe spend cap resets on a daily boundary, so the correct response to the warning is to stop consuming and resume the following day.\n\n## Plan\n\n1. Add guidance to `AGENTS.md` instructing agents to stop starting new billable LLM work when the daily Bedrock spend warning is active, and to resume the next day. The guidance must state the response, not the threshold value.\n2. Define \"stop\" precisely so it is actionable and does not strand work: finish or abandon the in-flight gate, do not start another, and record the pause on the ticket being worked so the next session can resume from a known state.\n3. Document the pollable signal an agent can read to detect the condition without waiting for the SNS notification, since agent sessions are not SNS subscribers.\n4. Cross-reference the existing gate-cost guidance in `AGENTS.md` so the pause rule sits with the other operating limits rather than in a new orphan section.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- **No cost figures, thresholds, or spend amounts in any committed file.** The `tickets` branch auto-pushes to the public GitHub mirror, and the guidance itself lives in a public repo. Refer to the threshold by name (the configured warning threshold), never by value. A prior redaction on 2026-09-12 removed tickets for exactly this reason.\n- The rule must be portable: it cannot depend on a specific CI provider, and an agent with no AWS credentials must still be able to follow the written instruction.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `AGENTS.md` instructs agents to pause new billable LLM work when the daily Bedrock spend warning is active and to resume the following day.\n- [ ] The guidance names the pollable detection signal and the operation that reads it.\n- [ ] The guidance defines what \"pause\" means for in-flight versus not-yet-started gate operations, including how to record the pause so work resumes cleanly.\n- [ ] No threshold value, dollar amount, or other cost figure appears in any file changed by this ticket.\n- [ ] The guidance is amended into existing operating-limit guidance rather than added as a standalone section.\n","id":"ec87-4e9d-c92d-4be8","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Pause agent work until the next day when the Bedrock daily spend warning fires"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1789668213459036993,"uuid":"882f1a7c-419e-42c1-a235-51396becbc6c"}